WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.434 size:75% position:38%
-Our next guests are
entertainment icons

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:03.069 size:78% position:39%
who have been married
for over 40 years.

00:00:03.069 --> 00:00:06.906 align:start size:94% position:6%
She's an award-winning
actress, author, and activist,

00:00:06.906 --> 00:00:08.341 line:92%
and he is a talk show legend

00:00:08.341 --> 00:00:11.745 size:78% position:39%
New episodes of their
podcast "Double Date"

00:00:11.745 --> 00:00:12.445 size:81% position:41% line:92%
are available Mondays.

00:00:12.445 --> 00:00:16.016 align:start size:94% position:6%
Please welcome to the show
Phil Donahue and Marlo Thomas.

00:00:16.016 --> 00:00:18.718 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you both so much
for being here.

00:00:18.718 --> 00:00:19.786 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hi, hi.
-Hi.

00:00:19.786 --> 00:00:21.955 align:start size:94% position:6%
Seth! I've never
been up this late.

00:00:21.955 --> 00:00:24.357 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I'm very
honored to have you.

00:00:24.357 --> 00:00:27.093
And you know, I wish I had
all my guests in studio,

00:00:27.093 --> 00:00:28.895 align:start size:94% position:6%
but Phil, this would have
been extra special.

00:00:28.895 --> 00:00:32.732 align:start size:94% position:6%
You used to film
your show in this studio.

00:00:32.732 --> 00:00:34.768 line:92%
Do you have fond memories of 8G?

00:00:34.768 --> 00:00:39.272
-Well, have you noticed my ghost
wandering around there?

00:00:39.272 --> 00:00:44.544 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. We've never seen a ghos
with such a long mic cord.

00:00:44.544 --> 00:00:48.548
-Right. Right. No kidding.
That was the early days.

00:00:48.548 --> 00:00:51.251 align:start size:94% position:6%
I used to run to
the back of the audience

00:00:51.251 --> 00:00:55.321 align:start size:94% position:6%
and strangle three people
in the front row.

00:00:55.321 --> 00:00:57.290 align:start size:94% position:6%
That was before
the wireless mic.

00:00:57.290 --> 00:00:58.458 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, obviously
hosting a talk show

00:00:58.458 --> 00:01:02.762 align:start size:94% position:6%
paid off as well for you, Phil
specifically with Marlo.

00:01:02.762 --> 00:01:05.298 align:start size:94% position:6%
I did not realize you guys hav
been together for 41 years

00:01:05.298 --> 00:01:09.235
and you met, Marlo, when you
were a guest on Phil's show.

00:01:09.235 --> 00:01:13.606 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. Yeah. It was kind o
love at first sight.

00:01:13.606 --> 00:01:15.909 align:start size:94% position:6%
Or something.
Something chemical happened.

00:01:15.909 --> 00:01:20.346
He came into the green roo
and I had not seen his show,

00:01:20.346 --> 00:01:22.949 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause it wasn't
in L.A. at the time.

00:01:22.949 --> 00:01:23.583 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And so he came in,

00:01:23.583 --> 00:01:26.319
and it was like one of those
shampoo commercials, you know?

00:01:26.319 --> 00:01:30.590
The white hair and the blu
eyes, the whole Irish thing.

00:01:30.590 --> 00:01:33.526 line:92%
I got very interested in him

00:01:33.526 --> 00:01:39.032 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he looked at me and said -
[ Chuckles ] --

00:01:39.032 --> 00:01:42.168 size:88% position:44%
-Well, I thought she was
a bad thought, you know?

00:01:42.168 --> 00:01:45.839 align:start size:94% position:6%
If you're Catholic, you
understand what that means

00:01:45.839 --> 00:01:46.706 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Laughing ]

00:01:46.706 --> 00:01:52.545 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And one thing led to anothe
and before you know it,

00:01:52.545 --> 00:01:54.614 line:92%
we were a real, live couple.

00:01:54.614 --> 00:01:56.783 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But I read that
you met your wife

00:01:56.783 --> 00:01:58.718 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you fell in love
at first sight.

00:01:58.718 --> 00:02:03.289 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That is the way
I agreed to tell it.

00:02:03.289 --> 00:02:05.959 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughing ]
No, but I mean, that's --

00:02:05.959 --> 00:02:06.626 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-It is true, though.

00:02:06.626 --> 00:02:09.863 align:start size:94% position:6%
We met at a wedding
and the last thing

00:02:09.863 --> 00:02:13.166 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think either of us
were looking for was that,

00:02:13.166 --> 00:02:16.236 align:start size:94% position:6%
and yet we're together
ever since then,

00:02:16.236 --> 00:02:20.773 align:start size:94% position:6%
so it is amazing
how fortuitous it can be.

00:02:20.773 --> 00:02:21.674 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-And a lot of people

00:02:21.674 --> 00:02:25.145 align:start size:94% position:6%
that we interview for
the podcast, that was so.

00:02:25.145 --> 00:02:27.280 line:92%
Billy Crystal was like 18.

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:28.448 line:92%
He was playing ball on the beach

00:02:28.448 --> 00:02:31.384 align:start size:94% position:6%
and this girl in
a pink bikini walked by

00:02:31.384 --> 00:02:32.852 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he, like,
fell in love with her,

00:02:32.852 --> 00:02:35.655 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they've been married,
like, 60 years.

00:02:35.655 --> 00:02:37.223 size:75% position:38% line:92%
So that does happen.

00:02:37.223 --> 00:02:43.196 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The first vision --
Malcolm Gladwell made this

00:02:43.196 --> 00:02:47.066 align:start size:94% position:6%
a part of American culture
really.

00:02:47.066 --> 00:02:54.407
The first look at a person
is the most important one.

00:02:54.407 --> 00:02:56.809 line:92%
That's when -- well, we foun

00:02:56.809 --> 00:03:00.013
in the interviews we did
with couples for our book,

00:03:00.013 --> 00:03:07.053 align:start size:94% position:6%
many of those couples
fell in love on the first date

00:03:07.053 --> 00:03:08.988 align:start size:94% position:6%
the first look,
the first anything.

00:03:08.988 --> 00:03:13.893 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And I was doing his show,
so it was kind of bare,

00:03:13.893 --> 00:03:15.028 line:92%
because we'd never met before,

00:03:15.028 --> 00:03:17.630 align:start size:94% position:6%
and all of the sudden
we were flirting like mad,

00:03:17.630 --> 00:03:21.267 align:start size:94% position:6%
and his show was
one person for an hour,

00:03:21.267 --> 00:03:22.302 size:88% position:44% line:92%
and you know, I'm going,

00:03:22.302 --> 00:03:23.937 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Oh, Phil.
You're so funny, Phil."

00:03:23.937 --> 00:03:27.473
It was just really embarrassing,
but it happens,

00:03:27.473 --> 00:03:29.375 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I'm sure you felt that
when you met Alexi.

00:03:29.375 --> 00:03:33.880 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I did. I want to ask, because
I will say the next day --

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:35.281 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know,
we met Friday of a wedding

00:03:35.281 --> 00:03:36.115 line:92%
and the wedding on Saturday --

00:03:36.115 --> 00:03:39.452
true stories, people were coming
up and asking my wife and I,

00:03:39.452 --> 00:03:41.888 align:start size:94% position:6%
who had just met,
how long we'd been a couple.

00:03:41.888 --> 00:03:46.125 align:start size:94% position:6%
So it was chemistry right away
but I'm wondering --

00:03:46.125 --> 00:03:46.926 line:92%
you guys knew you were flirting,

00:03:46.926 --> 00:03:49.729
but friends of yours who
watched that TV appearance

00:03:49.729 --> 00:03:52.999 line:92%
did they recognize it as well?

00:03:52.999 --> 00:03:53.967 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Everybody.
-Yeah.

00:03:53.967 --> 00:03:56.803 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Everybody called me and said,
"What was that about?"

00:03:56.803 --> 00:04:00.773 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, it wasn't
my first talk show, right?

00:04:00.773 --> 00:04:01.507 size:84% position:42% line:92%
I'd been interviewed by

00:04:01.507 --> 00:04:03.309 align:start size:94% position:6%
Johnny Carson
and all other people.

00:04:03.309 --> 00:04:06.980 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'd never fallen for anybody
on their show before.

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:07.547 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It was just --

00:04:07.547 --> 00:04:10.316
and the woman that lived
next door to you came over

00:04:10.316 --> 00:04:11.884 line:92%
and she said that to you.

00:04:11.884 --> 00:04:13.119 align:start size:94% position:6%
She said,
"What did you do today?

00:04:13.119 --> 00:04:18.591
-Yeah. Well. You know, "Wh
was that you had on today?

00:04:18.591 --> 00:04:21.427 align:start size:94% position:6%
So you know,
I guess it was obvious.

00:04:21.427 --> 00:04:23.196 line:92%
We didn't think so at the time

00:04:23.196 --> 00:04:24.897 line:92%
We weren't thinking about that

00:04:24.897 --> 00:04:29.602
-But he called me the next day
and then we went out to dinner

00:04:29.602 --> 00:04:30.837 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
That was it.

00:04:30.837 --> 00:04:32.472 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Ta-da.
-Ta-da. There you are.

00:04:32.472 --> 00:04:34.907 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You guys were
pretty private early on.

00:04:34.907 --> 00:04:38.611 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, for being a couple
that had a profile,

00:04:38.611 --> 00:04:39.712 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, each of you
were well-known.

00:04:39.712 --> 00:04:43.783 align:start size:94% position:6%
You were not very public about
your relationship, correct

00:04:43.783 --> 00:04:45.218 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-No, we haven't been.

00:04:45.218 --> 00:04:46.753 line:92%
And we made the decision early

00:04:46.753 --> 00:04:50.623 align:start size:94% position:6%
because we got married quietly
in my parents' house

00:04:50.623 --> 00:04:52.925 size:75% position:38%
and then we took off
for our honeymoon.

00:04:52.925 --> 00:04:53.926 size:88% position:44% line:92%
And so when we got back,

00:04:53.926 --> 00:04:57.297 align:start size:94% position:6%
we were being asked to
co-host the Emmys together

00:04:57.297 --> 00:05:00.633 align:start size:94% position:6%
and co-host, what was it,
the People's Choice,

00:05:00.633 --> 00:05:04.604
and "People" magazine and
it was kind of alarming.

00:05:04.604 --> 00:05:07.707 align:start size:94% position:6%
We said to each other,
"Let's back off from this,

00:05:07.707 --> 00:05:10.009 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause if we do this,
we're putting it out there

00:05:10.009 --> 00:05:13.579 align:start size:94% position:6%
like a product, and they'l
just take shots at it,

00:05:13.579 --> 00:05:14.480 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
so let's be quiet."

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:19.052 align:start size:94% position:6%
So we did. We kept our
marriage out of the limelight.

00:05:19.052 --> 00:05:20.186 line:92%
We didn't do anything together

00:05:20.186 --> 00:05:23.323 align:start size:94% position:6%
But then after being married
like, about 39 years,

00:05:23.323 --> 00:05:25.425 align:start size:94% position:6%
we thought,
"Well, they can't hurt us now.

00:05:25.425 --> 00:05:26.125 line:92%
What are they gonna say?"

00:05:26.125 --> 00:05:29.395
-They say, wait 40 years, and if
you're still happily married

00:05:29.395 --> 00:05:30.730 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
do a podcast.

00:05:30.730 --> 00:05:32.565 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But it was fun,
because there we were

00:05:32.565 --> 00:05:35.802 align:start size:94% position:6%
for the first time,
talking about our marriage

00:05:35.802 --> 00:05:38.404 align:start size:94% position:6%
on these double dates
with these other people,

00:05:38.404 --> 00:05:40.506 line:92%
and it was a new experience.

00:05:40.506 --> 00:05:42.208 size:84% position:42%
And Phil had said to me
when we were starting

00:05:42.208 --> 00:05:44.444 align:start size:94% position:6%
to go out around the country
to interview the couples,

00:05:44.444 --> 00:05:47.380 align:start size:94% position:6%
he said, "I'm not talking
about our marriage."

00:05:47.380 --> 00:05:47.947 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I said, "Okay."

00:05:47.947 --> 00:05:51.017
When you're married 40 years
you know what to say, right?

00:05:51.017 --> 00:05:51.884 size:78% position:39% line:92%
I said, "No problem."

00:05:51.884 --> 00:05:56.823
But once we got there, you did
because it was a conversation.

00:05:56.823 --> 00:06:01.928 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, if I said
anything about us,

00:06:01.928 --> 00:06:04.597 align:start size:94% position:6%
it seemed to
blow the doors open.

00:06:04.597 --> 00:06:06.699 line:92%
The other couple would --

00:06:06.699 --> 00:06:11.371 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, it's like we couldn'
get them to stop talking.

00:06:11.371 --> 00:06:16.909 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think there's
a message there somewhere --

00:06:16.909 --> 00:06:21.948 align:start size:94% position:6%
four people are
more likely to say things

00:06:21.948 --> 00:06:26.452 align:start size:94% position:6%
that are more intimate
than two people.

00:06:26.452 --> 00:06:28.388 line:92%
-Than a reporter would get

00:06:28.388 --> 00:06:32.625 align:start size:94% position:6%
A lot of people who
interviewed us afterward

00:06:32.625 --> 00:06:35.495 align:start size:94% position:6%
from newspapers and magazine
and stuff said,

00:06:35.495 --> 00:06:37.897 size:88% position:44%
"How did you get them to
talk about these things?

00:06:37.897 --> 00:06:38.698 line:92%
I could never have gotten that."

00:06:38.698 --> 00:06:41.501 size:88% position:44%
I said, "Well, you're a
reporter, and we're not.

00:06:41.501 --> 00:06:43.436 align:start size:94% position:6%
We're a couple."
-[ Chuckles ] Right.

00:06:43.436 --> 00:06:44.570 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So we're sitting down
with another couple

00:06:44.570 --> 00:06:46.939 align:start size:94% position:6%
over a glass of wine
and talking.

00:06:46.939 --> 00:06:48.841 align:start size:94% position:6%
It doesn't have
that scary feeling

00:06:48.841 --> 00:06:50.443 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you're going to
be misquoted

00:06:50.443 --> 00:06:52.412 line:92%
and somebody's out to get you.

00:06:52.412 --> 00:06:54.714 line:92%
We didn't have any of that

00:06:54.714 --> 00:06:57.784 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Based on the people
you've talked to,

00:06:57.784 --> 00:07:00.253 line:92%
are there any main takeaways

00:07:00.253 --> 00:07:03.156 align:start size:94% position:6%
Any keys that you feel
you've discovered

00:07:03.156 --> 00:07:04.891 line:92%
about a healthy relationship

00:07:04.891 --> 00:07:09.362 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-I think in many ways,

00:07:09.362 --> 00:07:14.534 align:start size:94% position:6%
we discovered things that
we should have already known

00:07:14.534 --> 00:07:17.904 line:92%
but first of all, it takes both.

00:07:17.904 --> 00:07:23.443 align:start size:94% position:6%
You can't have one person
committed to the relationshi

00:07:23.443 --> 00:07:24.444 size:75% position:38% line:92%
and the other person

00:07:24.444 --> 00:07:27.613 size:78% position:39%
like baggage that has
to be dragged along.

00:07:27.613 --> 00:07:33.986 align:start size:94% position:6%
That wears out the person
who's for the union,

00:07:33.986 --> 00:07:35.154 line:92%
and the other one who isn't.

00:07:35.154 --> 00:07:37.523 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So all of these
long-married couples,

00:07:37.523 --> 00:07:40.126 align:start size:94% position:6%
they all had
this thing in common,

00:07:40.126 --> 00:07:43.463
which is they both really
wanted it, whatever it was

00:07:43.463 --> 00:07:47.800
Kyra Sedgwick said there can b
no Plan B when you get married

00:07:47.800 --> 00:07:48.334 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
This is it.

00:07:48.334 --> 00:07:50.636 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they go to
marriage counseling --

00:07:50.636 --> 00:07:52.805 align:start size:94% position:6%
not Kyra Sedgwick,
but many of the couples

00:07:52.805 --> 00:07:53.606 line:92%
went to marriage counseling.

00:07:53.606 --> 00:08:02.615
-Yeah, I think that is the
ultimate, I think, evidenc

00:08:02.615 --> 00:08:05.718 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
of a good marriage.

00:08:05.718 --> 00:08:09.489 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, if people
are voluntarily

00:08:09.489 --> 00:08:15.595 align:start size:94% position:6%
committed to marriage
counseling,
that means you really care

00:08:15.595 --> 00:08:16.496 line:92%
-We've never been to one,

00:08:16.496 --> 00:08:19.565 align:start size:94% position:6%
because Mr. Irish here
would rather die

00:08:19.565 --> 00:08:21.234 size:88% position:44% line:92%
than talk about himself.

00:08:21.234 --> 00:08:22.768 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He'll go if
it's court-appointed,

00:08:22.768 --> 00:08:25.738 line:92%
but he's not going voluntarily

00:08:25.738 --> 00:08:26.205 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Right.

00:08:26.205 --> 00:08:29.842
-You guys, thank you so much
both for doing the podcast

00:08:29.842 --> 00:08:31.577 align:start size:94% position:6%
and for spending time
with me today.

00:08:31.577 --> 00:08:33.012 size:84% position:42% line:92%
I really appreciate it.

00:08:33.012 --> 00:08:33.980 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Thank you, Seth.

00:08:33.980 --> 00:08:36.816 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Good luck on your marriage.
-Thank you.

00:08:36.816 --> 00:08:40.386 align:start size:94% position:6%
-New episodes of "Double Date"
are available Mondays.

